  m_Name: LiquidRingCompressorData
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  engineName: 'Liquid Ring Compressor '
  engineDescription: A Liquid Ring Compressor is a rotary compressor that uses a
    rotating liquid ring to compress gases and is particularly suitable for applications
    requiring reliable gas handling and sealing. It operates using an eccentrically
    mounted impeller inside a casing partially filled with sealing liquid, usually
    water or another compatible fluid. Its major components include the casing, impeller,
    shaft, liquid ring, inlet and outlet ports, bearings, and mechanical seals. During
    operation, the rotating impeller causes the liquid to form a ring around the
    casing. Because of the eccentric position of the impeller, the spaces between
    the impeller blades and liquid ring continuously change in volume, drawing gas
    in and compressing it before discharge. Liquid ring compressors are widely used
    in vacuum systems, chemical processing, refrigeration, petroleum industries,
    and gas handling. From an engineering perspective, liquid-ring formation, sealing
    effectiveness, gas compression, liquid temperature, cavitation, corrosion, and
    power consumption are important factors affecting performance.
  engineCategory: Engineering
